From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: clamp indirect gpu_prerast fans to the arena on v10+
 biblioklept

Indirect triangle fans are not in the GPU chunk loop, so gpu_prerast
lowers them in one pass. With more vertices (times instances) than the
arena holds, the lowered VS skips the records past record_capacity and
writes no generated index past 65536, but the generated raster draw,
the XFB kernel, the GS kernel and the polygon kernel still used the
API counts: the triangles past the arena were drawn from stale records
and indices of earlier draws.

A one-invocation kernel (panlib_fan_clamp_draw, new fan_chunks.cl) now
runs on the compute queue after the CS has stored the indirect counts
and before the lowered VS. If vertices x instances is over the record
capacity, it clamps the vertex count to the capacity and the instance
count to capacity / vertices in the VS params, the VS dispatch grid and
the generated draw. Every consumer reads those words, so the record
layout stays consistent: the first triangles are drawn right and the
rest is dropped. Draws that fit are unchanged (the kernel returns).

Still open: indirect fans over 2048 instances that fit the arena run as
one grid (the G615 hang size), the primitives generated query counts
the clamped draw. Both go away with the fan chunk loop (next patch,
opt-in).

The new kernel lives in its own file so draw_helper.cl, which jm-v9
patches later in the series, keeps its lines.

Build-only; not device-tested.

Generated-by: LLM
